# Build products of the LaTeX source. The `.tex` is what is versioned; everything
# below is regenerated by pdflatex on every compile, so committing it would put a
# binary in the history that nobody can diff and that goes stale on the next edit.
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.pdf
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# Word conversions. The `.tex` is the source of truth; a `.docx` exists to be handed to
# reviewers who need to edit prose in a tool they already have. It is a DERIVATIVE, and
# committing it would create a second document that drifts from the first the moment
# somebody edits one and not the other — with no way to tell which is current.
# Their edits come back as changes to the `.tex`, not as a newer binary.
*.docx
